    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high-ceiling production today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score makes him our clear standout. Facing Hughes, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and favorable SP skill data (+17%), cementing him as the core of our lineup. Following closely is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), who, despite the \"Lineup Pending\" designation, gains significant utility from a favorable wind-out condition and a strong platoon edge against Rodriguez. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Hughes for our middle-of-the-order bats; **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Coby Mayo** are locked in to exploit the favorable SP_xERA, even with slight negative platoon adjustments for **Coby Mayo**. While **Henry Bolte** and **Luis Lara** draw tougher matchups against Gore and Boyd respectively, their efficiency scores remain above our 40-point floor, justifying their inclusion to maintain daily game caps.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves the benching of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (49.45). Despite his pedigree, the matchup against Williams (2.97 xERA) suppresses his output to the point where he falls below the efficiency floor of our active starters. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** was the clear first-man-out, losing ground due to the significant SP skill penalty associated with facing an elite arm. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Kyle Tucker** and **Heliot Ramos**; both carry strong scores (70.31 and 65.75, respectively), but their final projection is tethered to the assumption of favorable order placement. **Jackson Merrill** remains a high-value play not just for his raw projection, but for the added stolen base upside provided by the slow delivery of Lodolo, a critical factor in our strategy to bolster our scarcest category. Be advised that while we are aggressive today, the risk of lineup changes for players like **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** warrants a final check shortly before first pitch to ensure we aren't burning a game cap on a non-starter.",
